In apps/api/src/task/validate-task-fields.ts add a valibot import and three exports.
Add at the top with the other imports: import * as v from "valibot";
Append these exports verbatim at the end of the file:

export const MAX_ESTIMATED_HOURS = 10_000;

export const estimatedHoursSchema = v.pipe(
  v.number("Estimated hours must be a number"),
  v.finite("Estimated hours must be a finite number"),
  v.minValue(0, "Estimated hours cannot be negative"),
  v.maxValue(
    MAX_ESTIMATED_HOURS,
    "Estimated hours cannot exceed " + MAX_ESTIMATED_HOURS,
  ),
  v.transform((value) => Math.round(value * 100) / 100),
);

export const nullableEstimatedHoursSchema = v.nullable(estimatedHoursSchema);

export const optionalEstimatedHoursSchema = v.optional(
  nullableEstimatedHoursSchema,
);

Use a template literal for the maxValue message rather than string concatenation if that matches the file's style. Change nothing else in the file.

Five coupled edits in apps/api/src/task/index.ts. They must all land together or the file will not compile.

1. IMPORTS. Add: import updateTaskEstimatedHours from "./controllers/update-task-estimated-hours";
   in the existing alphabetically-sorted controller import block (between updateTaskDueDate and updateTaskPriority).
   Extend the existing "./validate-task-fields" import to also bring in nullableEstimatedHoursSchema and optionalEstimatedHoursSchema alongside VALID_PRIORITIES.

2. POST /:projectId. Add estimatedHours: optionalEstimatedHoursSchema, to the validator("json", v.object({...})). Add estimatedHours to the handler destructure of c.req.valid("json"). Pass estimatedHours, into the createTask({...}) call. Change the describeRoute description to "Create a new task in a project, optionally with an estimate in hours".

3. PUT /:id. Add estimatedHours: optionalEstimatedHoursSchema, to the validator("json", ...). Add estimatedHours to the handler destructure. Replace the positional updateTask(...) call with the named-object form: await updateTask({ id, title, status, startDate: parsedStartDate, dueDate: parsedDueDate, projectId, description, priority, position, userId, currentUserId, estimatedHours }). Change the describeRoute description to "Update all fields of a task, including its estimated hours".

4. NEW ROUTE. Insert a new .put(...) link immediately AFTER the "/due-date/:id" block and BEFORE the "/title/:id" block:
  .put(
    "/estimated-hours/:id",
    describeRoute({
      operationId: "updateTaskEstimatedHours",
      tags: ["Tasks"],
      description: "Update only the estimated hours of a task",
      responses: {
        200: {
          description: "Task estimated hours updated successfully",
          content: { "application/json": { schema: resolver(taskSchema) } },
        },
      },
    }),
    validator("param", v.object({ id: v.string() })),
    validator("json", v.object({ estimatedHours: nullableEstimatedHoursSchema })),
    workspaceAccess.fromTask(),
    requireWorkspacePermission({ task: ["update"] }),
    requireEntitlement,
    async (c) => {
      const { id } = c.req.valid("param");
      const { estimatedHours } = c.req.valid("json");
      const currentUserId = c.get("userId");
      const task = await updateTaskEstimatedHours({ id, estimatedHours, currentUserId });
      return c.json(task);
    },
  )

5. POST /import/:projectId. Add estimatedHours: optionalEstimatedHoursSchema, to the per-task object inside the tasks: v.array(v.object({...})) validator.

Do not change any other route, middleware order, or operationId.

Append one exported formatter to apps/web/src/lib/format.ts, reusing the file's existing private getLocale helper:

export function formatEstimatedHours(value: number, locale?: string) {
  return new Intl.NumberFormat(getLocale(locale), {
    maximumFractionDigits: 2,
  }).format(value);
}

maximumFractionDigits: 2 is what absorbs float artifacts, so 0.30000000000000004 renders as "0.3".
Add no imports. Change no existing function.

Create apps/web/src/lib/estimated-hours.ts. Pure module: no React, no i18n, no side effects, no imports except a type-only import if needed.

export const MAX_ESTIMATED_HOURS = 10_000;

export function sumEstimatedHours(tasks: Array<{ estimatedHours?: number | null }>): number
  Sums estimatedHours across tasks. A task whose value is null or undefined contributes 0.
  Round the final total to 2 decimals so 0.1 + 0.2 returns exactly 0.3, never 0.30000000000000004.

export type ParsedEstimatedHours = { ok: true; value: number | null } | { ok: false };

export function parseEstimatedHoursInput(raw: string): ParsedEstimatedHours
  - empty or whitespace-only input -> { ok: true, value: null }   (empty is NOT zero)
  - "0" -> { ok: true, value: 0 }
  - a finite number >= 0 and <= MAX_ESTIMATED_HOURS -> { ok: true, value: <rounded to 2dp> }
  - anything else (non-numeric, negative, above the max, NaN, Infinity) -> { ok: false }
  Use Number(trimmed) and Number.isFinite; do not use parseFloat, which would accept "2abc".

Create apps/web/src/fetchers/task/update-task-estimated-hours.ts mirroring update-task-due-date.ts exactly.

import { client } from "@kaneo/libs";

async function updateTaskEstimatedHours(taskId: string, estimatedHours: number | null) {
  const response = await client.task["estimated-hours"][":id"].$put({
    param: { id: taskId },
    json: { estimatedHours },
  });
  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.text();
    throw new Error(error);
  }
  return await response.json();
}

export default updateTaskEstimatedHours;

Pass estimatedHours straight through - null must reach the API as null so it clears the estimate. Do NOT coerce with || or ??. Do not create any parallel request layer.
